  "diagnosis": "The only failing check is dmft_subspace_model_window, and it fails on the model's make-up, not its accuracy. The RMS on the target states is 0.51 meV against a 20 meV limit. The deck builds 26 functions per spin from Ni 3d+4s+4p and O 2s+2p, but the DMFT target is Ni 3d plus O 2p, which is 16. The repair keeps only Ni d1 (3d) and O 2p. It also moves the O 2s bands (9-10), isolated 10.6 eV below the valence, into the bottom exclusion; otherwise they would be frozen with no function to hold them. Finally it lowers dis_froz_max from 2.26 to 1.53 eV so the frozen window ends just above the top of band 26 (1.524 eV) and below band 27 (from 1.535 eV at \u0393). At 2.26 eV the window holds 17 states for 16 functions. validate_deck accepts the deck: num_wann 16, num_bands 94, exclude_bands 1-10 honoured by the gate, at most 16 frozen states.",
